# MuPDF Android Viewer

This project is a simplified variant of the full MuPDF Android app that only
supports viewing documents. The annotation editing and form filling features
are not present here.

This project builds both a viewer library and a viewer application.
The viewer library can be used to view PDF and other documents.

The application is a simple file chooser that shows a list of documents on the
external storage on your device, and hands off the selected file to the viewer
library.

## Changes in this fork

The viewer library has been reworked for comfortable reading on a phone:

* The status and navigation bars are hidden while reading, so the document
  has the whole screen. They reappear together with the toolbars when you
  tap the page, and the page slider then sits above the navigation bar.

* Pages are stacked vertically and scroll continuously from one to the next,
  rather than paging sideways. Tapping the left or right edge of the screen
  still moves by a page height. A flick turns the page even when it sweeps
  up to 45 degrees off vertical, as a thumb tends to.

* Double tapping toggles between fitting the page width and fitting the
  whole page. Any pinch zoom is dropped so the new fit applies immediately.

* Text can be selected: press and hold to select a word, then drag either of
  the handles to adjust the selection, and Copy to put it on the clipboard.
  This only works where the document really contains text; pages whose
  lettering is drawn as artwork have nothing to select.

* Hyperlinks are always live. The link highlighting toggle that used to be
  needed to follow them has been removed from the toolbar.

* A share button hands the document to another app, and a download button
  saves a copy of it to the phone's Downloads folder. Both are hidden for
  documents that were not opened from a content: uri.

* Markdown files (.md) open too, laid out like an ebook so the font size
  button applies. The bundled MuPDF already renders them; the viewer just
  had to claim the text/markdown type and recognise the file name.

* The toolbars and the page slider are half again as tall as they were, and
  the slider is centred in its bar. Dragging the slider turns to that page
  as you drag instead of waiting for you to let go.

The application has its own id, io.github.ngjhd.mupdf, instead of Artifex's
com.artifex.mupdf.viewer.app, so Google Play no longer offers the upstream
viewer as an update to it. It installs alongside a copy built with the old id
rather than replacing it.

The application module has one other build change: the build produces a single
arm64-v8a APK. That is the architecture of every modern Android phone, and it
is the only artifact published on the GitHub releases page. The stock build
also emitted armeabi, mips, mips64 and riscv64 APKs which contain no native
library at all and crash as soon as a document is opened, along with 32 bit,
emulator and universal APKs that nothing here needs.

